{title: 460 - As Water to the Thirsty}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #460 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 460}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]As water [Am]to the thirsty, [F/C]as [Dm]beauty [F]to the eyes,
[F/A]As strength [C7/E]that [Am]follows weakness, [F]as [Am]truth instead [Edim]of [F]lies,
[F]As [Bb]songtime [C7/E]and springtime [F]and [Dm]summertime [Gm]to be,
[C7/E]So [Am]is my [F]Lord, [Dm]my [Gm]living [Edim]Lord [C]so [Dm]is my Lord [Gm]to [F]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Like calm [Am]in place [F/C]of [Bb]clamor
[C]Like [C7/E]peace [Am]that [F]follows pain,
[F/A]Like meeting [Am]after parting,
[F]Like [Gm]sunshine [F]after [Gm]rain;
[F]Like [Bb]moonlight [C7/E]and starlight [F]and [Dm]sunlight [Gm]on the sea,
[F]So [Bb]is [C7/E]my Lord, [F]my [Dm]living [Gm]Lord,
[C7/E]So [Am]is [Dm]my [Edim]Lord [Dm]to me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]As sleep [Am]that follows [Bb]fever,
[F/A]As [C7/E]gold [Am]instead of [Edim]grey,
[F/A]As freedom [Am]after bondage,
[F]As [Gm]sunrise [F]to [Gm]the day;
[F]As [Bb]home [Gm]to [C7/E]the trav'ler [F]and [Dm]all [Gm]he longs to see,
[C7/E]So [Am]is my [Dm]Lord, [Gm]my [Edim]Living [Dm]Lord to [Gm]me.
{end_of_verse}
